---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro'
---

<Layout 
  title="A-Level Exam Strategy Guide | Free Timing, Revision & Paper Tips"
  description="Complete A-Level exam strategy guide with timing, revision techniques, and paper-specific tips. Free download for A-Level students."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <h1>A-Level<br><span>Exam Strategy Guide</span></h1>
    <p>Timing, revision techniques, and paper-specific tips. Maximize your A-Level results.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Revision Planning</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Timetable Structure</h3>
        <pre><code>12 weeks before exam&#58;
  Weeks 12-9&#58; First pass (broad)
  Weeks 8-5&#58;  Second pass (depth)
  Weeks 4-1&#58;  Past papers
  Week 0&#58;     Light review only

Study 4-6 hours per day max</code></pre>
      </div>
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Active Recall Methods</h3>
        <pre><code>1. Blurting&#58; Write all you know
2. Flashcards&#58; Test yourself
3. Past papers&#58; Under timed conditions
4. Teach someone else
5. Interleave topics (mix them up)</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Exam Timing Strategy</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Time Allocation</h3>
        <pre><code>Rule&#58; 1.5 minutes per mark
6-mark question = 9 minutes
12-mark question = 18 minutes
25-mark essay = 37 minutes

Read all questions first (5 min)
Allocate time before writing</code></pre>
      </div>
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Paper-Specific Tips</h3>
        <pre><code>• Short answer&#58; be precise
• Long answer&#58; plan before writing
• Show all working for calculations
• Include units in final answers
• Check significant figures</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Answering Extended Questions</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Essay Structure</h3>
        <pre><code>Introduction (1 mark)&#58;
  Define terms, state argument

Body (8-10 marks)&#58;
  Paragraph 1&#58; AO1 + AO2
  Paragraph 2&#58; AO1 + AO2
  Paragraph 3&#58; AO3 evaluation

Conclusion (1-2 marks)&#58;
  Clear, justified judgment</code></pre>
      </div>
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Linking Sentences</h3>
        <pre><code>• "This suggests that..."
• "However, research shows..."
• "A strength of this is..."
• "A limitation is..."
• "Overall, the evidence suggests..."</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Common Mistakes</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Avoid These</h3>
        <pre><code>1. Not reading the full question
2. Spending too long on Q1
3. Not answering what is asked
4. Forgetting to evaluate
5. Missing units or sig figs
6. Not leaving time to review</code></pre>
      </div>
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Last-Minute Checklist</h3>
        <pre><code>□ Read every question twice
□ Check mark allocations
□ Write answers in full sentences
□ Include evaluations (AO3)
□ Check units and sig figs
□ Review if time remains</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Download</h2>
    <p>Print this page or save as PDF for quick reference.</p>
    <p><strong>Tip:</strong> Use Ctrl+P (Cmd+P on Mac) to print or save as PDF.</p>
  </section>
</Layout>
